      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "The number of targets you can destroy is infinite.\n\nSPOLERS BELOW\n\n[color=white]Runes of Malediction + Relic Spirit combo.\n\n[color=white]Fixer: Jack Handle, Alternating Tiger Claw, Harmony, Bloody Knuckles\n\n[color=white]Legacy: Inspiring Prescence + Galvanize\n\n[color=white]Visionary: Twist the Ether x2- Mr. Fixer\n\n[color=white]Insula Primalis-Obsidian Field\n\n[color=white]Fixer deals 9 irreducable damage to the runes, which revive the relic spirit, which revive the runes again. Assuming this isn&#39;t just a silly loophole to the puzzle, this should count as destroying as many targets as possible in a turn. This kind of damage should K.O. nearly every target with at least 9 HP without worrying about damage reduction, so I don&#39;t know how many targets that would be.[/color][/color][/color][/color][/color][/color]\n",
